  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Earmuff mode has shown to be immensely useful for focusing in on conversations or quieting busy instances. I've seen lots of friends start using it. It would just be great to toggle it from the launchpad as soon as you need it. Right now, it can take a bit to turn on Earmuffs.\nCurrently if you want to enable Earmuffs, you have to click another QM tab and scroll down. You can disable it easily with the top bar, but not enable it. If you're having trouble with audio and need Earmuffs on, it takes far too long to dig through the menu to activate it. \nSo why not add it to the Launchpad for easy access? Just a small Earmuffs button for toggling it on and off. I feel like it would best placed either by the mic toggle in the bottom left or maybe somewhere on the top of the launchpad. It honestly just needs to somewhere that allows users to quickly use it instead of having to dig around in the menu.\nIt would also help newer users learn that it's a feature if it's just on the launchpad. They can start using it sooner and create a better experience for themselves early on",
